From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Validate the packing with a type that is 8 bytes on
 Windows too

PhysX checks that the application has not set the pack value below 8 by
asserting that a long follows a char at offset 8 in a struct, and picks
that long for every clang that is not compiling for 32 bit arm. A long is
4 bytes on Windows, where clang is not only clang-cl: with llvm-mingw the
compiler is clang and the data model is LLP64, so the assertion fails,
and it is in PxPreprocessor.h, which means it fails in every translation
unit of the build.

Leave the Windows compilers the long long that the fallback already uses
for MSVC, which is 8 bytes wherever PhysX builds. The long is there for
the unices, where it is the type whose alignment -malign-double does not
have to be asked for; that reasoning never applied to Windows.

The assertion holds for x86_64 and arm64 llvm-mingw, for clang-cl, which
takes the MSVC path and was never affected, and for the Linux, arm,
Android and WebAssembly targets, which keep the branch they had.
---
 src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxPreprocessor.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxPreprocessor.h b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxPreprocessor.h
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxPreprocessor.h
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxPreprocessor.h
@@ -471,7 +471,7 @@ PX_CUDA_CALLABLE PX_INLINE void PX_UNUSED(T const&)
 // This assert works on win32/win64, but may need further specialization on other platforms.
 // Some GCC compilers need the compiler flag -malign-double to be set.
 // Apparently the apple-clang-llvm compiler doesn't support malign-double.
-#if PX_APPLE_FAMILY || (PX_CLANG && !PX_ARM)
+#if PX_APPLE_FAMILY || (PX_CLANG && !PX_ARM && !PX_WINDOWS_FAMILY)
 	struct PxPackValidation
 	{
 		char _;
